sentences.t:
et nunc lenta manu spargens hastilia denset,
nunc validam dextra rapit indefessa bipennem;
aureus ex umero sonat arcus et arma Dianae.

sentences.l:
and now, pliant, from her hand scattering javelins, she thickens them,
now the stout in her right hand she snatches, unwearied, double axe;
golden from her shoulder rings the bow, the arms of Diana.

sentences.t:
His addit Amastrum
Hippotaden, sequiturque incumbens eminus hasta
Tereaque Harpalycumque et Demophoonta Chrominque;

sentences.l:
To these she adds Amastrus,
son of Hippotes, and she pursues, leaning on, from afar, her spear,
Tereus and Harpalycus and Demophoon and Chromis;

“Foolish Ligurian, and in vain in spirit lifted up, proud,
for nothing your fathers' you have tried, slippery one, arts,
nor will trickery you unharmed to deceitful carry home Aunus,”
